type: thesis
title: "Stiff-sloppy spectra and systematic reduction of high-dimensional cancer-state ODEs under gated observation maps"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  Which directions of a high-dimensional cancer-state parameter space are
  sloppy under realistic observation maps, and can a documented MBAM /
  Fisher-geometry reduction preserve the gated claims of the full model
  without silently renaming leftover sloppy combinations as biology?
  A ten-parameter, four-state toy is observed either as log viable burden
  or as a laboratory split into proliferating, quiescent and apoptotic
  cells. Bulk data have practical Fisher rank 3 of 10 and an exact null
  in apoptotic clearance. The laboratory map raises practical rank to 6
  of 10 and leaves the stress product as the stiff combination. A
  quasi-steady reduction keeps the late burden claim. A flow that moves
  apoptosis along a flat canyon, and a rebound term that spends the null
  clearance coordinate, do not. Synthetic generator, seed 20260921.
  Not a medical device.
keywords:
